  <static seed="118" source="Contrib/METU-NCC/MAT101/Derivatives/Linear_approx.pg">
    <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)</m> is a function with <m>f(-3) = -3</m> and 
<m>f'(-3) = 3</m>.</p>
<p><alert> A.</alert> <m>\quad</m> Give the equation of the 
tangent line to <m>y=f(x)</m> at <m>x=-3</m></p>
<p><m>\quad y =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> B.</alert> <m>\quad</m> Estimate the following values.</p>
<p><m>\quad \displaystyle f\left(-2\right) \approx</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>\quad \displaystyle f\left(-4\right) \approx</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-3+3\mathopen{}\left(x-\left(-3\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
